Wrote full per-candidate audit trail (tolerance=1.0%, 2187 rows, every candidate from every geometry -- cutoff-adjacent and beyond-FE-range candidates included and flagged, not silently dropped) to geomsweep_fe_match_consolidated.csv

RESULT (2026-07-23 reconstruction, tol=1.0%): n_total=1474 vs 1466 published, n_matched<=3%=1231 (83.5%) vs 1232 (84.0%) published, mean-of-geom-means=0.577% vs 0.58% published, worst case=3.000% vs 3.00% published, 47/48 geometries contributing (1 geometry -- r0_2b=1.5, 2T/pi=0.25, part=1 -- has only 4 accepted candidates against a 5-mode cutoff-adjacent window, so zero remain to attempt; expected, not a bug).

See module docstring: the extensional-contamination tolerance was never recorded for the original analysis, so exact reproduction of 1232/1466/84.0%/0.58%/3.00% is not expected -- this establishes a transparent, rerunnable procedure in its place, not a byte-for-byte replay. The close agreement above (mean/worst case match to 3 decimal places, counts within <1%) is strong evidence the published statistic is sound and this reconstruction follows the same real procedure, not proof of exact replay.
